WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-ES

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.420
Hello.  Welcome back
to Lam Rim.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:12.760
Today we're going to do a review
of the entire course.  It's

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:13.860
good for me.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:17.020
I'd like to do a review myself.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:20.960
This format of producing the episodes
separately

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:24.520
and then doing them at different times

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:27.600
seems to lose the flow of the entire
teaching.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.600
I thought it would be nice if today we went back to

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.800
the beginning and flowed

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.600
through all the teachings of Lam Rim
that we have had.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.340
I'm going to flow in that way based
on the idims,

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.580
the idea-images,

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:47.580
that we use to teach
ACI teachers.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.740
ACI teachers are expected to be

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:53.460
able to look at one
of these images

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:55.660
and identify the idea behind it.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:01:00.800
I think... Tim, how many did we say there would
be?  A thousand or something like that?

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.660
How many?

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:09.720
Something like 500.
So it's easy to take the test,

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:12.360
to examine someone based solely
on photos,

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.360
so we're only presenting you with
these photos.

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:18.180
So I challenge you during this review:

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:21.460
when we put up a picture, I'll

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:26.560
give you a second and see if you can remember
what the picture was about.  Alright

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:28.820
?  This is a good review

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:33.580
of the entire course we are doing.
Okay, here we go.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:38.380
First image Mr. Sejii.

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:42.620
This image is supposed to
remind you

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:47.660
that we are halfway through the practices

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:50.020
for average-ability people,

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:53.660
and what they are trying to achieve is nirvana.  They are

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:55.700
trying to get off the Wheel
of Life,

00:01:55.700 --> 00:02:00.280
out of all personal suffering.

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:03.560
This is where Buddha taught
the three trainings

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:07.520
that will help you reach
your personal nirvana.

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:12.780
The third training is understanding emptiness,
understanding the feather.

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:16.100
The second training is meditation.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:20.100
At a deep level, these two
can only be done

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:23.740
in a quiet place, during certain
times of the day,

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:28.300
when you are really focusing
on your meditation mat.

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:34.220
At a deep level, these two should be done
during special times of the day,

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.400
but this one,

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:39.940
the basis of the other two, which is being kind
to people,

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:41.860
you can call it morality,

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:44.560
you could call it an ethical lifestyle,

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:49.300
but in the end it is being kind to people.

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:54.040
That is the foundation we always have
at our disposal all day long.

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:58.420
This is one of the three extraordinary trainings
of Buddhism,

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:01.300
in order to help us achieve nirvana.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:04.140
And we have it available all day.

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:06.180
So, in this image

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:10.380
you can see Seiji helping Geshe Michael
to decrypt his computer.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:16.160
Which is one of the nicest things young people
can do for older people.

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:18.540
Next image.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:23.120
See if you can remember
what this image was.  Did

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:27.420
you guess?

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:30.520
This lady is paying her taxes.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:34.120
What does this make it in the
Lam Rim system?  It

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:35.900
makes her...

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:39.100
a Dharma teacher.

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:42.180
When I say Dharma master,
or tantric master, I

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:44.540
already know the image you have in your mind:

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:49.260
it's a great lama on a throne
with a big yellow hat,

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:52.400
maybe they're ringing a bell

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:57.820
and a small drum and they're...

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.760
and you think, "'Oh, he's a Dharma master,
he's a real Dharma master.'"

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:04.920
Or you're thinking about that old picture
of Nagarjuna,

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:07.880
and it's all very mystical.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:12.000
But in truth, in Lam Rim,
what we learned

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.940
was about this woman.

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:18.320
She has two children, is married,

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.800
and is a Dharma teacher.

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:22.760
She is a true Dharma master.

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:24.340
Pabongka Rinpoche said,

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:28.880
"Don't think that a Dharma master
has to be sitting on a throne

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:30.840
reciting some tantric ritual."

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:34.740
This lady is doing... what?  He

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:37.720
is paying his taxes.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:43.820
Being honest with your taxes
is really difficult in my country.  It

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:46.900
can take weeks to prepare
your taxes,

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:49.260
to prepare them carefully,

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:51.700
to do them with complete honesty,

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:54.460
to pay every penny you're supposed to
pay.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:56.600
This makes her...

00:04:56.600 --> 00:05:01.260
She has the first of the
extraordinary trainings of a good person, to

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:02.940
be kind to people,

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:05.440
and that makes her a true
Dharma master.

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:07.920
Forget those images you have

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:09.920
of lamas with big hats,

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:14.640
and ringing bells.  That's easy,
anyone can do that.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:17.540
Being kind to people is difficult,

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:22.200
and maintaining your morality, maintaining
your ethics, is also difficult.

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:24.960
The next one.  I'll

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:32.640
give you a moment.  Do you remember
what this is about?

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.120
The quote in the Lam Rim was:

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:39.220
(TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA'I DGE SLONG
'OD DANG LDAN)

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:42.880
A person who is really keeping
his vows,

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:47.720
really keeping his Buddhist guidelines,
especially the ten rules,

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:50.220
shines, really shines.

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:59.100
A person who is making a healthy,
modest, and discreet effort to keep their commitments,

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:02.080
to maintain the ten good karmas, to

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:04.300
be kind to people,

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:08.400
has a calm look on their face,

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.440
is glowing.

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:12.380
When they enter a room, you know it,

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:15.120
everyone starts to feel better.

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:17.620
Like Tim and Seiji.

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:19.920
That is a light in the world.

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:25.000
Buddha said, "Those people are the light
of the world."

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:27.060
There is a Christian expression:

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:30.500
Don't put a candle in a basket.

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:33.780
Let the world see your happy face.

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:37.360
And that is a light,

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:41.020
a true guiding light for the whole
world.

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:45.100
Next image.  Idim number 4

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:54.920
Yes. This is a cliff I went to
with my partner Veronica

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:58.940
for her birthday, during this Lam Rim.  They

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:03.680
were talking about the sunset,

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:07.420
whose word in Tibetan is (NUB PA).  It is

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:10.480
also the word for west,
because the sun sets in the west.

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:13.940
So (NUB PA) means:
the sunset.

00:07:13.940 --> 00:07:16.960
And this is a very sad verb.

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:21.400
This is a very sad idea in the Dharma.

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:25.580
The most famous place is at the end
of the Abhidharmakosha,

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:27.920
The Treasury House
of Higher Wisdom.

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:31.040
The Treasure House of Higher Knowledge,
of Master Vasubhandu,

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:32.780
and he says:

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:39.100
"The sun of Dharma, the light of Dharma,
will be hidden in this world."

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:41.840
We will lose the light of the Dharma
in this world.

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:44.000
This world will enter into darkness.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:46.300
After a certain time,

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:49.760
the Buddha's teachings will disappear
from this world.

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:54.760
First they disappear from
people's minds,

00:07:54.760 --> 00:07:57.500
but they will still be in libraries; those books
are still in libraries.

00:07:57.500 --> 00:08:00.380
Probably in libraries that John Brady has
not yet found.

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:06.840
And later they will also disappear from libraries,
and then they will disappear completely.

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:11.180
I put the photo here because Pabongka Rinpoche
made a special observation,

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:13.240
saying,

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:17.500
"If you cannot keep your commitments,
if you cannot maintain

00:08:17.500 --> 00:08:20.000
'good behavior with people,

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:23.200
' then we can say that the Dharma
has left this world.

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:27.740
The light of the Dharma has left this world
within you."  "

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:30.860
The sun has set inside
your own chest."

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:34.740
Which would be a very sad thing,
if we don't keep our vows.

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:38.540
Next picture.

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:49.460
Yes. We called this retreat Love
in the Time of the Virus.

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:55.660
The point was that during a
very difficult time in the world,

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:57.600
if you keep your commitments,

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:01.100
if you are kind to people

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:04.340
when things are scary,
frightening, the virus is spreading, we do

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:06.880
n't know where, we don't know how, we do

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:10.900
n't know how many people are going to
die...

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:14.460
If during those difficult times

00:09:14.460 --> 00:09:16.880
you do something good for other people, it

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:19.440
is much, much more powerful.

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:23.380
He mentioned, if you remember, a 5-star Buddha paradise.

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:26.460
Which is like a perfect place,

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:30.580
it's easy to be a good person, everyone
there is a good person.

00:09:30.580 --> 00:09:32.600
That's not a great achievement. It's not

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:35.780
the big deal, and the seed
isn't that powerful,

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:38.840
being kind in a group
of nice people.

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:43.840
Being kind when people are attacking you,
when people are afraid,

00:09:43.840 --> 00:09:48.560
when people aren't being kind to each
other, and being the one person

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:54.160
who stands up and shares things
in a difficult time,

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:58.280
then  That is an extremely pure person.
That is great karma.

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:01.240
That is incredible karma,
much more powerful.

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:04.620
I think the virus is a very good
time,

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:09.280
a very good opportunity
for all of us to show: Are

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:11.560
we truly Buddhists? Are

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:15.020
we truly practicing the
bodhisattva path?

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:19.620
Can we help others even when things
are so difficult?

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:22.340
Next image.

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:31.100
This one is hard to remember; I have difficulty
recalling it. I'll

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:36.320
give you a second to try to think
about what this image is.

00:10:40.600 --> 00:10:45.020
Okay. Pabongka Rinpoche was quoting
some books

00:10:45.020 --> 00:10:49.080
with a very, very common ending
from different books.

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:51.740
He quoted a famous one, which says:

00:10:51.740 --> 00:10:56.760
(BLO BZANG RGYAL BA'I BSTAN PA CIG)
(BLO BZANG RGYAL BA'I BSTAN PA CIG). It

00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:58.080
means:

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:03.700
"May the teachings of the Victorious

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:06.140
Lobsang Drakpa, Je Tsongkhapa,

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:09.320
be spread throughout this world."

00:11:09.320 --> 00:11:13.380
And you're thinking,
"We have to go online,

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:17.340
we have to translate this Lam Rim
into many languages."  We must

00:11:17.340 --> 00:11:22.920
try to spread the good word
to as many people as possible."

00:11:22.920 --> 00:11:27.940
That's the end of the sentence, and we're supposed to
leave

00:11:27.940 --> 00:11:31.320
this Lam Rim class or video

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:35.420
and share the Dharma
with people.

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:38.480
And we are supposed to spread the Dharma
throughout the world.

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:44.580
And in this part of the Lam Rim,
Pabongka Rinpoche said, "Look,

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:47.180
the place where you're supposed to spread
the Dharma

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:50.860
is here, inside your own heart."

00:11:50.860 --> 00:11:54.480
Don't think that spreading
the Dharma means

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:58.660
trying to translate the videos into more languages
or something like that.

00:11:58.660 --> 00:12:01.480
That's a very important spreading
of the Dharma,

00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:05.960
but he says, "If you spread it
in your own heart,

00:12:05.960 --> 00:12:08.140
then of course it will spread
out of you."

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:10.320
Because the world comes from your heart.

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:12.920
From your heart chakra, actually.

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:17.760
Next picture, number 7.

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:22.220
Try to remember what
this picture was about. I'll

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:25.240
give you a second.

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:32.920
Yes. This is one of my favorite themes,

00:12:32.920 --> 00:12:39.440
having a personal relationship
with another person,

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:43.680
like the one these two people have.

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:48.060
In my opinion, and in Tantra, it's one of the
happiest things that can happen to you.

00:12:48.060 --> 00:12:52.780
It's one of the most wonderful things
that can happen to you.

00:12:52.780 --> 00:12:58.400
Anyone can tell you that the reason
everyone is looking for a partner

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:02.080
is because it makes people happy; it's one
of the greatest blisses.

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:04.440
When everything is going well,

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:07.260
it's one of the  the greatest joys you
can have.

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:13.560
But, you and I know that when it's not right, it's

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:17.000
one of life's greatest miseries.

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:22.060
Why is this relevant to this course here?

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:29.320
If your morals are good,

00:13:29.320 --> 00:13:32.060
it's the happiest thing in your life.

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:34.260
And if you break your morals,

00:13:34.260 --> 00:13:36.720
it's the same thing that will make you miserable.

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:41.280
It's like having a good woman or man
as your partner;

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:47.460
the same person who makes you totally happy
can also make you totally miserable.

00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:50.320
So in this case, Vinaya,

00:13:50.320 --> 00:13:54.480
your personal practice of kindness,
good behavior,

00:13:54.480 --> 00:14:00.460
is being compared to a partner
who can make the best thing in your life,

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:03.760
or the worst thing in your life—the same person.

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:08.020
Next idim. Number 8, I think.

00:14:11.520 --> 00:14:15.740
This was a tricky one. Let's see
if you can remember it.

00:14:15.740 --> 00:14:18.680
I'll take a sip of my green drink.

00:14:18.680 --> 00:14:21.640
Thank you, Vinaya.

00:14:26.140 --> 00:14:28.140
Yes.

00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:34.040
This really represents breaking
your commitments.

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:39.520
Pulling up a weed represents breaking
your commitments.

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:45.280
Why...? I mean, destroying this plant
is breaking your commitment.

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:52.480
If you're a gardener, you know you have to pull up
the weeds

00:14:52.480 --> 00:14:55.480
before the seeds are ready.

00:14:55.480 --> 00:14:59.960
If you wait until  So that the seeds are ready
to fall,

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:02.200
and then you pull up the plant,

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:05.780
you're going to scatter about a thousand seeds.

00:15:05.780 --> 00:15:08.800
By the next month or year,

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:11.220
you're going to have thousands of weeds
growing again.

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:14.480
So you have to attack those weeds
in advance.

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:22.020
This relates to a very radical statement
that the Buddha made,

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:27.440
(DGE SLONG DAG SROG DANG
BRAL ZHING SHI BA NI BLA'I)

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:33.700
It is better to die than to break your vows.
Why?

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:35.820
When you break your vows,

00:15:35.820 --> 00:15:39.200
you are setting in motion seeds

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:43.540
that will continue to fall for
many lifetimes.

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:48.940
If you die, you ruin one
body-mind set.

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:54.520
If you die, you ruin a very useful temple,

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:58.580
a physical temple and a mind.
You lose one.

00:15:58.580 --> 00:16:01.380
But if you break your commitments,

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:05.240
you lose many body-mind sets.

00:16:05.260 --> 00:16:08.360
You ruin your body and mind for many lifetimes.

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:14.340
And you kind of set in motion the seeds
that are going to ruin many lifetimes. The

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:16.960
Buddha was saying,

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:19.480
"It is better to die than to break your vows."

00:16:19.480 --> 00:16:23.100
And he wasn't being metaphorical.

00:16:23.100 --> 00:16:28.600
He was speaking very literally
when he said that.

00:16:28.600 --> 00:16:32.940
Better to die than to break your commitments.

00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:37.280
There's a joke in the Lam Rim.

00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:41.840
We take the  The vow not to renounce
bodhichitta,

00:16:41.840 --> 00:16:45.300
even at the cost of our lives.

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:48.900
There is a famous saying

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:52.800
that throughout our lives we
are waiting to be

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:57.220
thrown in jail by
some evil people.

00:16:57.220 --> 00:17:03.200
They come with a knife and say to you, "Renounce
your bodhisattva vows or die today."

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:06.560
So we're going to say, "I choose to die."

00:17:06.560 --> 00:17:09.800
And they kill us.

00:17:09.800 --> 00:17:14.260
I think we're all waiting... ever since
we took that vote, we've

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:18.460
all been waiting for these guys to show up
with knives and threaten us.

00:17:18.460 --> 00:17:20.920
But in reality, we're the guys
with knives.

00:17:20.920 --> 00:17:24.600
We threaten our bodhisattva vows
every day.

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:28.880
We have to make this decision every
day,

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:33.780
when we carefully decide whether or not to keep
our vows.

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:38.140
It's hard to find those types who throw you
in jail and say,

00:17:38.140 --> 00:17:42.280
"I'm going to kill you if you don't renounce
your bodhisattva vows."

00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:47.540
The following image

00:17:48.020 --> 00:17:50.220
is... See if you can remember it.  I'm

00:17:50.220 --> 00:17:55.440
going to give you a minute to try
to remember.

00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:06.460
This was a reference...

00:18:06.460 --> 00:18:09.860
we have the
"Mixed Nuts" translation team,

00:18:09.860 --> 00:18:13.960
and we were translating an ancient
Vinaya text,

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:17.160
monk's vows, nun's vows.  They

00:18:17.160 --> 00:18:22.720
were talking about the vow, the tradition

00:18:22.720 --> 00:18:25.920
that we shouldn't...

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:29.900
when you become a monk or nun, they
give you your robes, they

00:18:29.900 --> 00:18:33.000
give you a small Buddha statue

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:36.000
and they give you a strainer.

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:40.520
And in ancient India, you were supposed to bring
this strainer with you.

00:18:40.520 --> 00:18:44.080
When you drink water from a stream, you are supposed to

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:46.880
strain the water first

00:18:46.880 --> 00:18:51.440
to make sure you don't kill
any small insects.

00:18:51.440 --> 00:18:56.280
We mentioned a famous tradition
in the Vinaya,

00:18:56.280 --> 00:19:00.120
that if a couple of monks walk
towards the water,

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:02.660
to a stream to get some water,

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:08.680
then they must choose the friendliest monk
to check the water.

00:19:09.280 --> 00:19:13.260
Don't choose the one who doesn't care
about insects.

00:19:13.260 --> 00:19:16.080
Try to find someone who loves
insects

00:19:16.080 --> 00:19:20.460
and ask them to check the water.  Because they will be
more careful.

00:19:20.460 --> 00:19:22.980
What's the point?

00:19:22.980 --> 00:19:27.120
We're talking about a type of ecological vows,

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:30.620
where monks and nuns are
not even supposed to...

00:19:30.620 --> 00:19:32.580
pick green leaves from a plant,

00:19:32.580 --> 00:19:38.620
because they are the homes
of small creatures.  It

00:19:38.620 --> 00:19:43.220
means respecting even the
smallest votes,

00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:44.940
taking them very seriously

00:19:44.940 --> 00:19:49.940
because the results
multiply exponentially.

00:19:49.940 --> 00:19:56.520
So it's important to keep your morality
at a very subtle level, at a very fine level.

00:19:56.520 --> 00:20:00.600
And don't be picky.

00:20:00.600 --> 00:20:04.380
If I were to write the bodhisattva vows,
I would write an additional bodhisattva vow

00:20:04.380 --> 00:20:07.940
about not being fussy about your
bodhisattva vows.  There's

00:20:07.940 --> 00:20:12.400
nothing more irritating
than a person who...

00:20:12.400 --> 00:20:18.920
tells you they're keeping their vows and therefore
have to act like an idiot today.

00:20:19.760 --> 00:20:23.860
Keep your vows sweetly.  Keep them happy.  Do
n't exaggerate.

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:30.600
Don't bother people with your votes, because votes are
not meant to bother people.

00:20:30.600 --> 00:20:34.280
Keep the votes small, keep them
quiet, keep them personal,

00:20:34.280 --> 00:20:36.460
don't advertise them.

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:43.080
There is a saying in Islam: The left hand should not
know what the right hand is doing.

00:20:43.080 --> 00:20:47.460
It means, don't announce your votes.
Just keep them quiet.

00:20:47.460 --> 00:20:50.540
And keep them at a very fine level.

00:20:50.540 --> 00:20:54.060
Next image.

00:20:59.200 --> 00:21:05.100
This is the idea that being kind
to other people

00:21:05.100 --> 00:21:09.300
is like planting a tree.

00:21:09.300 --> 00:21:16.000
Oh, and today I went to the "Peach Tree Cafe"
to check something out, and

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:20.720
Stanley, Allison, and I planted a peach tree there


00:21:20.720 --> 00:21:24.520
when we started the "PeachTree Cafe
Morning Show".

00:21:24.520 --> 00:21:29.060
And I want to tell you that this week there were
three peaches

00:21:29.060 --> 00:21:33.080
and... we already have peaches!

00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:41.400
What it means is: take care of the foundation
of your practices, take care of the root,

00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:46.700
plant good karma by keeping your vows and
being kind to people.

00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:49.160
Then that will grow into a tree.

00:21:49.160 --> 00:21:53.780
And that peach tree that we planted,
about five months ago, is

00:21:53.780 --> 00:21:57.240
already bearing a lot of fruit.

00:21:57.240 --> 00:22:02.800
If you didn't take care of him when he was little, you wouldn't
have anything.

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:07.740
But if you take care of the foundation of your
Buddhist practice,

00:22:07.740 --> 00:22:10.060
which is being kind to people,

00:22:10.060 --> 00:22:12.920
then the fruits will be thousands
and thousands and thousands.

00:22:12.920 --> 00:22:17.260
It will come, and it will grow into a huge...
it will grow into a tree, it will bear

00:22:17.260 --> 00:22:22.680
peaches every year and for many years
you will have peaches.

00:22:22.680 --> 00:22:28.520
Keep, protect... this girl is
carefully protecting the outbreak.

00:22:28.520 --> 00:22:31.120
Protect your morality.

00:22:31.120 --> 00:22:33.960
Very good.  Next image.

00:22:34.880 --> 00:22:40.880
If I remember correctly, there were four conditions

00:22:40.880 --> 00:22:43.760
that could cause you to break
your commitments.

00:22:43.760 --> 00:22:46.520
If you took the Bodhisattva commitments

00:22:46.520 --> 00:22:49.800
or the Vinaya Pratimoksha commitments,

00:22:49.800 --> 00:22:54.780
or even if you took the Diamond Way commitments... tantric commitments.

00:22:54.780 --> 00:22:59.480
I think there were four of them.  Pabongka Rinpoche reviewed...
No, maybe more than that, anyway.

00:22:59.480 --> 00:23:03.500
There were certain conditions that would help you
break your vows.

00:23:03.500 --> 00:23:08.000
If you want to break your vows, there are some
special ways to do it.

00:23:08.000 --> 00:23:11.700
Here's the first one, which is:

00:23:11.700 --> 00:23:16.860
If you don't know what your votes are, then
that's a good way to break them.

00:23:16.860 --> 00:23:20.980
If you want to break them, then
don't study them.

00:23:20.980 --> 00:23:28.100
And one of my annoyances—I have many things
that bother me in the Dharma—

00:23:28.100 --> 00:23:32.040
is the teachers who give initiations,

00:23:32.040 --> 00:23:37.720
great initiations, and don't explain to the people
who are taking the initiation

00:23:37.720 --> 00:23:40.000
that they have just taken vows.

00:23:40.000 --> 00:23:44.360
There are hundreds of vows you take
when you have an initiation,

00:23:44.360 --> 00:23:47.400
and you're going to break them if you don't know them.

00:23:47.400 --> 00:23:50.820
It is the teacher's responsibility to

00:23:50.820 --> 00:23:55.400
train you on the vows before you
have an initiation.

00:23:55.400 --> 00:24:01.600
If they don't offer training, I wouldn't take
any initiation from them.

00:24:01.600 --> 00:24:06.180
The best way to break your vows, in the first place,
is not to know them.

00:24:06.180 --> 00:24:09.020
Read the recipe before you start cooking.

00:24:09.020 --> 00:24:12.660
That's what Veronica tells me every time I
cook.

00:24:12.660 --> 00:24:15.500
Next image.

00:24:15.520 --> 00:24:23.420
It's a lady saying, "Yes, it's not such a
big deal."

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:28.380
That vow of, I don't know...

00:24:28.380 --> 00:24:33.360
not cutting green plants without saying a prayer,

00:24:33.360 --> 00:24:38.520
"Come on, that's a little extreme.
It's a little excessive.

00:24:38.520 --> 00:24:44.480
That's not a big deal, it's just some insects
that might be using that leaf

00:24:44.480 --> 00:24:48.800
as a roof now and then,
so it's not a big deal."

00:24:48.800 --> 00:24:52.600
The second big way to break
your vows

00:24:52.600 --> 00:24:54.280
is to have this attitude:

00:24:54.280 --> 00:24:58.900
"Oh, that's not a big deal, I'm keeping
the bigger ones."

00:24:58.900 --> 00:25:02.140
Okay. Next up.

00:25:04.880 --> 00:25:11.400
If we have a klesha, meaning
if we have any kind of negativity

00:25:11.400 --> 00:25:16.020
circulating in our minds,
that's a great way to break your vows.

00:25:16.020 --> 00:25:18.760
Getting upset with someone,

00:25:18.760 --> 00:25:25.300
or obsessing over acquiring something, money,

00:25:25.300 --> 00:25:29.420
or clinging to our Netflix at night.

00:25:29.420 --> 00:25:37.500
That kind of... By the way, it's not wrong to watch Netflix,
but I'm talking about...

00:25:37.500 --> 00:25:41.760
hurting someone else because you want to get home
and watch Netflix. That's a problem.

00:25:41.760 --> 00:25:43.460
So,

00:25:43.460 --> 00:25:49.700
this is called "A Gang Fight,"
and the story is, what?

00:25:50.800 --> 00:25:55.580
Go after the big guy on the other side.

00:25:55.580 --> 00:25:58.180
Figure out who the leader on the other side is,

00:25:58.180 --> 00:26:03.280
and don't talk, don't negotiate, don't...  Scream,

00:26:03.280 --> 00:26:06.100
go up to him and hit him on the head.

00:26:06.100 --> 00:26:09.420
And then that whole side is going to fall apart.

00:26:09.420 --> 00:26:13.960
Identify your worst bad habit,

00:26:13.960 --> 00:26:19.640
and go after it first. That's the way
to keep your vows.

00:26:19.640 --> 00:26:22.720
The next one.

00:26:23.700 --> 00:26:26.360
If you...

00:26:26.360 --> 00:26:32.400
By the way, at the age of... my age, I'm not telling you
how old I am,

00:26:32.400 --> 00:26:35.760
but this whole young love thing

00:26:35.760 --> 00:26:40.960
is so ridiculous from my age's point of view
.

00:26:40.960 --> 00:26:45.020
And I can say that from experience because I've been through it
.

00:26:45.020 --> 00:26:46.880
But this thing of:

00:26:46.880 --> 00:26:50.080
"Oh, she's the most beautiful woman
in the world."

00:26:50.080 --> 00:26:53.700
"He's the most handsome guy in the world."

00:26:53.700 --> 00:26:57.640
First of all...

00:26:57.640 --> 00:27:02.180
my older brother said something really funny, he
said to me, "Do you like that girl?" I answered, "Yes."

00:27:02.180 --> 00:27:04.760
He said, "Do you want to spend your life with her?" I
said, "Yes."

00:27:04.760 --> 00:27:09.820
He said, "First go to her mother."  "Look at how
her mother looks."

00:27:09.820 --> 00:27:15.580
So I go over and the mother looks terrible. She's overweight, she
looks tired, she looks awful.

00:27:15.580 --> 00:27:23.360
And she said to me, "Well, how do you think she looked
at the beginning?"  So think about it.

00:27:24.080 --> 00:27:28.920
If you're attached to
a person's appearance,

00:27:28.920 --> 00:27:33.880
or something physical, or something not very important
about a person,

00:27:33.880 --> 00:27:37.400
that's going to change, and you're going to see them get
sick, you're going to see them

00:27:37.400 --> 00:27:42.960
age, you're going to see them get diarrhea
and vomit.

00:27:42.960 --> 00:27:47.640
If you're unlucky, you're going to see their insides in surgery
at some point.

00:27:47.640 --> 00:27:51.820
So don't fool yourself into thinking it's

00:27:51.820 --> 00:27:54.380
worth hurting other people

00:27:54.380 --> 00:28:00.520
to get the most beautiful woman or man
you can. It's not worth it. It wo

00:28:00.520 --> 00:28:04.440
n't last.

00:28:04.440 --> 00:28:07.960
It's great to have a relationship, but have it
for the right reason.

00:28:07.960 --> 00:28:10.600
Okay, next.

00:28:11.520 --> 00:28:14.660
If you have an anger problem

00:28:14.660 --> 00:28:17.000
or get annoyed easily,

00:28:17.000 --> 00:28:20.420
then fantasize about giving this person

00:28:20.420 --> 00:28:27.160
something they'll love having.
This is called maitri, jampa, love.

00:28:27.160 --> 00:28:30.880
Fantasize, try to remember
how nice it is to

00:28:30.880 --> 00:28:35.100
give someone something they love,
something they want,

00:28:35.100 --> 00:28:38.380
and try to have this attitude.

00:28:38.380 --> 00:28:41.560
If you don't feel friendly toward another person,

00:28:41.560 --> 00:28:45.520
then have fantasies—which means
meditation—

00:28:45.520 --> 00:28:50.320
about giving them something
they really like.

00:28:50.320 --> 00:28:52.740
The next one.

00:28:52.740 --> 00:28:54.380
It's... I'm

00:28:54.380 --> 00:29:00.020
going to give you a moment to  This one. I bet you ca
n't remember what this one is.

00:29:00.020 --> 00:29:05.260
Tim's cheating by looking ahead.

00:29:06.720 --> 00:29:09.700
What was this one again?

00:29:09.700 --> 00:29:13.460
Okay, this one's about pride.

00:29:13.460 --> 00:29:17.360
Pride is also going to be a hindrance
to keeping your vows.

00:29:17.360 --> 00:29:21.520
And one of the most common kinds of pride

00:29:21.520 --> 00:29:27.640
in a monastic setting, which is where
this book was taught,

00:29:27.680 --> 00:29:35.540
is: How much do you know about the scriptures?
How many events have you accumulated in your life?

00:29:35.540 --> 00:29:40.700
And this is something I really enjoy, the unknown events of the Dharma,

00:29:40.700 --> 00:29:45.400
and the more you accumulate, the more you feel
like you're special.

00:29:45.400 --> 00:29:48.260
And Pabongka Rinpoche said,

00:29:48.260 --> 00:29:51.680
"All the Dharma you have learned in your life,
all the things you have memorized,

00:29:51.680 --> 00:29:57.080
all the things you have debated,
all the degrees of Geshe you could have,

00:29:57.100 --> 00:30:01.820
compared to what you have left to learn, you
know nothing."

00:30:01.820 --> 00:30:07.460
You're like a worm at the bottom of the sea."

00:30:07.460 --> 00:30:11.940
And sometimes you come up and see the stars.

00:30:11.940 --> 00:30:15.220
Many of those stars have planets around them.


00:30:15.220 --> 00:30:21.340
There are people on those planets. There are things
to know about those people.

00:30:21.340 --> 00:30:26.260
The things we know that we're
so proud to know

00:30:26.260 --> 00:30:34.020
are a very, very, very small fraction
of what you could know.

00:30:34.020 --> 00:30:35.840
So don't be proud.

00:30:35.840 --> 00:30:38.400
Next.

00:30:41.680 --> 00:30:46.360
One of the biggest motivations
for breaking your vows

00:30:46.360 --> 00:30:50.780
or your commitments, your morality, which will prevent you from
reaching nirvana,

00:30:50.780 --> 00:30:57.220
which will prevent you from reaching the second level
of Lam Rim, personal nirvana,

00:30:57.220 --> 00:31:00.760
is understanding emptiness, studying emptiness.

00:31:00.760 --> 00:31:05.540
If you realize that the bad things

00:31:05.540 --> 00:31:08.260
someone is doing to you

00:31:08.260 --> 00:31:12.500
are coming directly from what you did
last week,

00:31:12.500 --> 00:31:17.620
then you're not going to make big mistakes.
The more you can study emptiness,

00:31:17.620 --> 00:31:21.920
the more you can study cause and effect,
dependent origination,

00:31:21.920 --> 00:31:24.880
which means, "That person comes
from my seeds,"

00:31:24.880 --> 00:31:30.820
then it's going to be easier to keep
your vows. It's going to be easier.

00:31:30.820 --> 00:31:34.200
So study, study, study. I

00:31:34.200 --> 00:31:37.440
had a teacher,  He said...

00:31:37.440 --> 00:31:41.140
an old Mongolian master,

00:31:41.140 --> 00:31:45.360
very old, with tuberculosis.

00:31:45.360 --> 00:31:48.040
He used to say:

00:31:48.040 --> 00:31:55.620
"He is very good.  You're so proud, you have
a lot of Princeton pride,

00:31:55.620 --> 00:32:00.320
"and then the Geshe thing, that's very useful,
very useful.

00:32:00.320 --> 00:32:05.140
" So you'll push yourself harder
just to look smart.

00:32:05.140 --> 00:32:10.500
"That's fortunate, but later on,
try to give that up.

00:32:10.500 --> 00:32:12.720
Just study to be a good person."

00:32:12.720 --> 00:32:15.040
It's very funny.  He gave me

00:32:15.040 --> 00:32:18.520
Adam's text
on his deathbed.

00:32:18.520 --> 00:32:21.740
I remember this.

00:32:22.560 --> 00:32:25.280
The following

00:32:26.160 --> 00:32:30.440
is technically the fourth cause, is it
?  No, whatever.

00:32:30.440 --> 00:32:34.680
One of the reasons for breaking your vows
or losing your commitments

00:32:34.680 --> 00:32:38.840
is that it is very difficult in the modern world

00:32:38.840 --> 00:32:43.140
to keep your mind on your vows when you are
very busy.

00:32:43.140 --> 00:32:45.360
When things are moving
very fast

00:32:45.360 --> 00:32:48.280
and there are a thousand things to see on the internet,

00:32:48.280 --> 00:32:51.620
and life is moving very fast,

00:32:51.620 --> 00:32:56.960
it's difficult to maintain that self-awareness

00:32:56.960 --> 00:33:02.860
of: "Am I breaking my vows, am I doing
something to hurt someone?"

00:33:02.860 --> 00:33:07.680
So you need to slow down,
return to your vows,

00:33:07.680 --> 00:33:13.680
and maintain some kind of sensitivity, some
awareness,

00:33:13.680 --> 00:33:18.680
to the fact that you have commitments
not to hurt people.

00:33:18.680 --> 00:33:23.560
The busier things get,
the more careful you have to be.

00:33:23.560 --> 00:33:25.980
It's easy to have... It

00:33:25.980 --> 00:33:30.100
's even easy to get annoyed with your partner
when you're very busy.  They're

00:33:30.100 --> 00:33:32.520
trying to tell you something

00:33:32.520 --> 00:33:36.420
and you have ten things happening
at work,

00:33:36.420 --> 00:33:41.420
and you're like, "Look, I don't have time
to listen to you right now.

00:33:41.420 --> 00:33:45.100
My boss gave me ten things to do."

00:33:45.100 --> 00:33:47.920
Those are the moments when you need to slow down


00:33:47.920 --> 00:33:49.960
and return to your vows,

00:33:49.960 --> 00:33:52.880
and don't forget your commitment to be kind
to people,

00:33:52.880 --> 00:33:57.900
even when you're very stressed,
very busy.

00:33:58.480 --> 00:34:02.420
It's better to break some

00:34:02.420 --> 00:34:08.020
business commitments than to get nervous, stressed, and unfriendly to people.

00:34:08.020 --> 00:34:13.720
It's better not to pay a bill or miss a business meeting

00:34:13.720 --> 00:34:18.020
or not do your best
at your job,

00:34:18.020 --> 00:34:22.100
if that means keeping
your mind clear.

00:34:23.600 --> 00:34:26.200
Next image.

00:34:26.200 --> 00:34:31.180
This is a lady buying something useless
in the store.

00:34:32.020 --> 00:34:35.440
See if you can remember this story.

00:34:35.440 --> 00:34:39.380
She said, "Oh, this box is very beautiful."  She
went to a department store.

00:34:39.380 --> 00:34:46.240
She bought this... What's it like?  What is that place
for the house, where you buy things?

00:34:46.240 --> 00:34:47.940
Crate and Barrel.

00:34:47.940 --> 00:34:50.340
She went to Crate and Barrel in the United States and
bought this.

00:34:50.340 --> 00:34:53.220
She said, "Oh, my husband is going to love this box
."

00:34:53.220 --> 00:34:56.660
She has no idea what she's going to use it for,

00:34:56.660 --> 00:35:00.480
but she's going to take it home.

00:35:02.960 --> 00:35:03.760
Then,

00:35:03.760 --> 00:35:08.440
when she gets home, her husband will say, "Are you crazy?
This is just a little box that's useless.

00:35:08.440 --> 00:35:11.960
We have enough junk in the house."  "

00:35:11.960 --> 00:35:14.420
Give it back, get your money back."

00:35:14.420 --> 00:35:21.200
Now, should I go to the gas station
and try to return it?

00:35:22.800 --> 00:35:29.500
No, that's not where she got the box.
It's obvious, but we have to mention it.

00:35:30.080 --> 00:35:32.880
If you buy a stupid box

00:35:32.880 --> 00:35:37.600
because you liked it and think your husband will
like it, which he won't,

00:35:37.600 --> 00:35:41.360
and he convinces you to return it,

00:35:41.360 --> 00:35:45.300
don't return it to a different place,
return it to the place where you bought it.

00:35:45.300 --> 00:35:48.380
What does that mean?

00:35:54.720 --> 00:35:57.360
You should pay me.

00:35:58.240 --> 00:36:02.160
When it's time to confess,
when you've broken a vow,

00:36:02.160 --> 00:36:06.240
then try to go back to the person
who gave you the vow.

00:36:06.240 --> 00:36:10.640
Try to confess in front of the person
who gave you the vow. Is

00:36:10.640 --> 00:36:15.600
it okay to confess at home alone?

00:36:16.240 --> 00:36:20.120
Not for vows you took from other people.

00:36:20.120 --> 00:36:22.560
Generally,

00:36:22.560 --> 00:36:25.960
if you didn't take a vow from someone else,

00:36:25.960 --> 00:36:27.960
then maybe it's okay to do it at home,

00:36:27.960 --> 00:36:33.080
confess in front of a Buddha statue or something,
in extreme cases it's okay.

00:36:33.080 --> 00:36:35.140
But generally,

00:36:35.140 --> 00:36:38.660
if you can go back to the person
who gave you your vows

00:36:38.660 --> 00:36:44.480
and confess to them  Openly, without shame.
We're shameless all day long.

00:36:44.480 --> 00:36:48.560
So, to be shameless about your vows,
just say, "What the hell."

00:36:48.560 --> 00:36:51.920
Go straight to your teacher and say,
"I tore up this stupid vow."

00:36:51.920 --> 00:36:56.160
And your teacher is like, "Wow!"  "You're a
very bad person!" And you say, "Yes, I am." Get over

00:36:56.160 --> 00:37:01.800
it. And then you feel so clean,
you feel so good. You

00:37:02.800 --> 00:37:06.480
can be shy about a lot of things
in your life, but don't be shy about your vows.

00:37:06.480 --> 00:37:09.880
If you break a vow, tell someone,

00:37:09.880 --> 00:37:13.160
and that's how you get rid of it.
You get rid of the problem.

00:37:13.160 --> 00:37:17.180
If you keep it and hide it, if you spend more time hiding it

00:37:17.180 --> 00:37:22.300
than confessing it, or holding onto it,
then it's just foolish,

00:37:22.300 --> 00:37:26.140
and you won't feel good, you won't feel clean.

00:37:26.140 --> 00:37:31.840
Just be upfront with your teachers:
"I have this problem."  "I have this bad habit."

00:37:32.220 --> 00:37:36.360
The karma is destroyed, the seed is destroyed.

00:37:37.080 --> 00:37:41.200
And you know, your teacher is going to say, "I've heard
that before, you've told me that before."

00:37:41.200 --> 00:37:45.440
But be persistent and keep telling them.

00:37:47.040 --> 00:37:49.780
Next picture.

00:37:50.400 --> 00:37:55.260
This one's about... wait, remember?

00:37:59.600 --> 00:38:06.260
Again, it's about honoring
the little details of vows.

00:38:06.260 --> 00:38:07.860
And they were talking...

00:38:07.860 --> 00:38:12.080
It's actually a vow for monks to
brush their teeth,

00:38:12.080 --> 00:38:14.940
with a stick, which was called (SO SHING).

00:38:14.940 --> 00:38:17.720
It was a stick that you were to use to clean your
teeth,

00:38:17.720 --> 00:38:22.980
and you just cut it from a tree
and use it. It's a toothbrush.

00:38:22.980 --> 00:38:29.680
And it's said that the monks should have their
toothbrushes and you should brush your teeth. It

00:38:30.400 --> 00:38:33.520
might seem like a small thing:

00:38:33.520 --> 00:38:38.200
"Wait, I'm trying to keep my
tantric vow to go to Amitabha's paradise

00:38:38.200 --> 00:38:39.860
and protect all living beings."

00:38:39.860 --> 00:38:44.900
And Buddha says, "Yes, but in the meantime, could you please
brush your teeth every day?"

00:38:44.900 --> 00:38:47.520
And you say, "But that's not a big vow."

00:38:47.520 --> 00:38:52.340
"Yes,  But it's the little things
that make up Buddha's paradise.

00:38:52.340 --> 00:38:59.860
It's the little things that bodhisattvas do,
the things that are kind to others.

00:38:59.860 --> 00:39:04.320
Of course, everyone in the world is
going to, I don't know...

00:39:04.320 --> 00:39:08.660
stop a nuclear war or something, if they can,
I mean, it's obvious.

00:39:08.660 --> 00:39:11.880
But are you a good enough person

00:39:11.880 --> 00:39:17.180
that you don't even want people to
smell your breath if it could hurt them?

00:39:17.180 --> 00:39:19.600
If you're very sensitive

00:39:19.600 --> 00:39:23.460
to the little things that could
hurt people,

00:39:23.460 --> 00:39:26.660
then we can say that you're upholding
your morals.

00:39:26.660 --> 00:39:32.820
And then it's the little details that give
the finishing touches

00:39:32.820 --> 00:39:37.900
to your Buddha's paradise, which you see
in the next picture.

00:39:40.620 --> 00:39:45.300
This is this person decorating a Christmas tree. I do

00:39:45.300 --> 00:39:48.680
n't know if you've ever put up a
Christmas tree,

00:39:48.680 --> 00:39:51.700
but those of us who grew up
in the Christian tradition had Christmas

00:39:51.700 --> 00:39:54.380
trees put up by our parents
.

00:39:54.400 --> 00:40:01.380
And there's something great about putting on the last ornament.

00:40:01.380 --> 00:40:06.720
Everyone is looking at the tree and they say,
"Is it done yet?" And they say, "Yes, it's done."

00:40:06.720 --> 00:40:10.740
Then they say, "Wait, there's one more
we should put on there."

00:40:10.740 --> 00:40:14.600
This Christmas ornament

00:40:14.600 --> 00:40:17.320
is the  Brushing your teeth.

00:40:17.320 --> 00:40:23.040
It's the little finishing touches you
put into your Buddhahood.

00:40:23.040 --> 00:40:26.960
It's the small things that make
Buddhas. It's

00:40:26.960 --> 00:40:29.860
not the grand things, it's not
the big things.

00:40:29.860 --> 00:40:33.760
It's paying attention to the small details

00:40:33.760 --> 00:40:38.100
of making people happy that creates
a Buddha.

00:40:38.100 --> 00:40:40.100
Very good.

00:40:40.160 --> 00:40:42.980
Next one.

00:40:44.160 --> 00:40:50.380
See if you remember this one. I'll give you a hint:
Yamantaka, Yamantaka.

00:40:55.780 --> 00:40:59.680
This is a famous story from the Lam Rim.

00:41:00.480 --> 00:41:05.580
Monks and nuns are supposed to attend
sojong twice a month and confess

00:41:05.580 --> 00:41:10.660
the mistakes they've made to each other
openly.

00:41:12.060 --> 00:41:13.940
The master said,

00:41:13.940 --> 00:41:17.860
"They hit the gunty.  They struck the gunty,

00:41:17.860 --> 00:41:21.920
which is a special piece of wood,
it looks like a 2x4 beam,

00:41:21.920 --> 00:41:26.700
and you strike it with another stick and it goes:
thunk, thunk, thunk.

00:41:26.700 --> 00:41:32.540
And that's a bell. That was an old bell,
before metal was common.

00:41:32.540 --> 00:41:38.240
They'll strike the board and when you hear that,
you have to go to sojong. They

00:41:38.240 --> 00:41:40.160
still do it.

00:41:40.160 --> 00:41:43.940
I made a gunty with my Master. He wanted one.

00:41:43.940 --> 00:41:48.820
We made it with the correct...
there are many rules about it.

00:41:48.820 --> 00:41:50.960
And when you hear the gunty, you're

00:41:50.960 --> 00:41:53.400
supposed to hold it here,

00:41:53.400 --> 00:41:56.620
hold the gunty here and stick it like this.

00:41:56.620 --> 00:42:00.800
Then all the monks
and nuns are supposed to come to confession.

00:42:00.800 --> 00:42:05.180
So, this master said,
"Hey, they struck the gunty."  "Let's go."

00:42:05.180 --> 00:42:09.100
The student said, "No, I'm not going to
confession today."

00:42:09.100 --> 00:42:11.180
The master said, "What?!"

00:42:11.180 --> 00:42:16.580
Because that is one of
a monk's main commitments, to go to sojong.

00:42:16.580 --> 00:42:20.060
The master said, "What are you talking about?"
He said, "I don't have to go today."

00:42:20.060 --> 00:42:22.180
The master said, "What do you mean you do
n't have to go today?"

00:42:22.180 --> 00:42:27.060
And he said, "You forgot that you gave me a
Yamantaka initiation yesterday."

00:42:27.060 --> 00:42:32.540
I am Yamantaka, I am a Buddha.  "I don't need to
go to sojong anymore."

00:42:32.540 --> 00:42:36.920
The master grabs him by the ear and says,
"What the hell are you, Yamantaka?"

00:42:36.920 --> 00:42:39.500
Yamantaka is going to go sojong with me right now
."

00:42:39.500 --> 00:42:42.520
"Ahhhh."

00:42:43.200 --> 00:42:47.600
What it means is: "Don't tell me these things
about you being a great tantrika,

00:42:47.600 --> 00:42:50.220
"and you're beyond morality

00:42:50.220 --> 00:42:53.900
and now you have a higher vision."

00:42:53.900 --> 00:42:57.480
It's a completely wrong idea.

00:42:57.480 --> 00:43:01.260
If you have a secret initiation,

00:43:01.260 --> 00:43:04.320
then you should go to sojong
every morning or something.

00:43:04.320 --> 00:43:07.000
You should go more than other people.

00:43:07.000 --> 00:43:08.780
Because that's what it gives you... that's what

00:43:08.780 --> 00:43:13.440
empowers your tantric practice:
being kind to other people

00:43:13.440 --> 00:43:15.960
and confessing when you make a mistake.

00:43:15.960 --> 00:43:19.060
Following.

00:43:21.580 --> 00:43:26.740
This is a sad image.  We
always think of morality

00:43:26.740 --> 00:43:31.900
as the roots of our practice,
the foundation of our practice.

00:43:31.900 --> 00:43:35.960
But Pabongka Rinpoche kind of turned it around
.

00:43:35.960 --> 00:43:41.100
This is a perfect image.
He said, "Imagine an apple tree

00:43:41.100 --> 00:43:46.060
that someone cut in half."  He
actually used the palm tree.

00:43:46.060 --> 00:43:51.300
Someone sliced ​​it up and cut off the
top of the tree.

00:43:51.300 --> 00:43:53.960
So you won't have any leaves,

00:43:53.980 --> 00:43:57.040
not even a single leaf will come out,

00:43:57.040 --> 00:44:00.080
therefore you won't get any flowers,

00:44:00.080 --> 00:44:04.460
and therefore you won't get the fruit
that always comes from the flowers.  You're

00:44:04.460 --> 00:44:06.700
not going to achieve anything.

00:44:06.700 --> 00:44:13.460
A person who is not kind to other people
day after day, hour after hour,

00:44:13.460 --> 00:44:18.640
cuts off any opportunity

00:44:18.640 --> 00:44:22.040
to reap those beautiful fruits
of practice.

00:44:22.040 --> 00:44:25.480
Very good.  The next one.

00:44:30.640 --> 00:44:35.840
This was an idea from something my Master
asked me... I'm

00:44:35.840 --> 00:44:43.260
sorry, I asked my Master and I don't know
if you remember, but I asked him:

00:44:43.260 --> 00:44:48.720
The first of the Five Paths,
the path of accumulation, you

00:44:50.040 --> 00:44:54.260
reach it when you have
a personal tragedy,

00:44:54.260 --> 00:44:58.040
but, if you are on the bodhisattva track you

00:44:58.040 --> 00:45:00.136
reach it when you obtain bodhichitta.

00:45:00.140 --> 00:45:05.700
I said, "I don't understand what is tragic
about bodhichitta."

00:45:05.700 --> 00:45:11.520
And he said to me, "'No, no, no. It's still a matter
of tragedy.

00:45:11.520 --> 00:45:18.840
It's just the tragedy of every living being;
every being in this universe

00:45:18.840 --> 00:45:22.020
has the same tragedy.'

00:45:23.180 --> 00:45:28.940
So, in truth, that communal tragedy
is the beginning of the Five Paths.

00:45:28.940 --> 00:45:31.180
Thinking about that tragedy

00:45:31.180 --> 00:45:36.300
is the beginning of the Five Paths for
a bodhisattva. So it really is the same thing.

00:45:36.300 --> 00:45:42.640
The puppy is having difficulties, but now all
the puppies in the basket are having difficulties.

00:45:42.640 --> 00:45:44.780
We're all in this together.

00:45:44.780 --> 00:45:47.880
And that's the beginning of bodhichitta.

00:45:50.880 --> 00:45:58.380
This next image is a man shaking
hands with someone in his office.

00:45:58.380 --> 00:46:04.600
I imagine the woman is introducing them: '
This is Joe; he works in the advertising department.'  "

00:46:04.600 --> 00:46:08.040
This is Sam, he works in the
IT department." They

00:46:08.040 --> 00:46:10.760
shake hands.

00:46:10.760 --> 00:46:14.120
Remember what this is?

00:46:18.060 --> 00:46:23.940
It was a really, really nice exercise where we were supposed to
close our eyes

00:46:23.940 --> 00:46:27.540
and think about the person who annoys us the most.

00:46:27.540 --> 00:46:32.380
And see if we could get angry.
The problem with this kind of exercise

00:46:32.380 --> 00:46:35.740
is that after about ten minutes
you forget it's an exercise,

00:46:35.760 --> 00:46:38.740
and you actually get angry.

00:46:38.740 --> 00:46:42.480
"Let me see if I can get angry."
"How are you going to do that?"

00:46:42.480 --> 00:46:47.060
"I'm going to think about this guy who made me angry
this week." "Okay, go ahead."

00:46:47.060 --> 00:46:50.920
Then, slowly, the person starts to tremble.
And you say, "What's going on?"

00:46:50.920 --> 00:46:56.080
"I got angry."  The experiment worked."

00:46:56.080 --> 00:46:59.700
If it's your Lama, they'll say,

00:46:59.700 --> 00:47:04.580
"Notice how you feel when you start
thinking about this person."

00:47:04.580 --> 00:47:08.200
How does it feel? What comes to your heart? I do

00:47:08.200 --> 00:47:11.760
n't know about you, but I feel a little unease
in my heart;

00:47:11.760 --> 00:47:17.240
I start to feel a kind of discomfort
here or there.

00:47:17.240 --> 00:47:22.280
When I think about a person who has been
bothering me or a problem that's bothering me,

00:47:22.280 --> 00:47:26.320
I can deliberately create tension

00:47:26.320 --> 00:47:28.880
within myself.

00:47:28.880 --> 00:47:35.920
He says, "Let's do an exercise.  Try to create
some tension in your heart,

00:47:35.920 --> 00:47:38.660
then observe that tension and become familiar with it.

00:47:38.660 --> 00:47:45.680
As if you were shaking someone's hand.
Learn what it feels like

00:47:45.680 --> 00:47:49.560
when a mental affliction,
a negative emotion,

00:47:49.560 --> 00:47:54.160
begins to rise in your heart,
and keep practicing.

00:47:54.160 --> 00:47:58.920
As soon as you feel better and forget
about this person, think about them again.

00:47:58.920 --> 00:48:02.600
See if you can get angry again. See if you can
start to get angry again.

00:48:02.600 --> 00:48:07.380
And try to familiarize yourself with what it feels like,
shake their hand: "Hello."  "He's Geshe Michael."

00:48:07.380 --> 00:48:09.660
"Hello, what's your name?"

00:48:09.660 --> 00:48:12.400
"I'm starting to get angry with this person."

00:48:12.400 --> 00:48:15.220
"Ah."  Pleased to meet you.  Now
I know what you look like.

00:48:15.220 --> 00:48:20.420
Now I can keep an eye on things.  "
I can avoid you in the future."

00:48:20.420 --> 00:48:23.700
Okay. Next up.

00:48:26.880 --> 00:48:30.980
It's called: Visiting the Center of the Sun.

00:48:31.520 --> 00:48:38.680
The theme of this Lam Rim, which was:
Love in the Time of the Virus.

00:48:39.600 --> 00:48:43.900
The virus is a big thing, it's spread all over
the world.

00:48:43.900 --> 00:48:47.800
I've lived a long life and thought I'd
seen it all.

00:48:47.800 --> 00:48:53.700
I entered my 60s and thought, "Well, now nothing
new is going to happen."

00:48:53.700 --> 00:48:56.800
"I'm pretty ready for anything
that might happen. I've

00:48:56.800 --> 00:49:00.700
seen it all, and nothing can bother me too much."

00:49:00.700 --> 00:49:05.220
Then this virus appears and threatens
everyone in the world.

00:49:05.220 --> 00:49:11.480
And I'm like, "Wow! That's huge,
that covers the whole planet."  I do

00:49:12.160 --> 00:49:17.280
n't know if it happened to you, but it happened to me.  It is
probably...

00:49:17.280 --> 00:49:22.100
negative action number nine,
which is ill will.

00:49:22.100 --> 00:49:24.240
Being happy when someone else has
a problem.

00:49:24.240 --> 00:49:30.420
When I heard that annoying, famous people were getting sick,

00:49:30.420 --> 00:49:33.680
I was like, [laughs] I did

00:49:33.680 --> 00:49:36.600
n't want them to die or anything,

00:49:36.600 --> 00:49:41.580
but I was like, "See? I told you it was bad
to be bad."

00:49:41.580 --> 00:49:45.740
And then I realized I was
thinking that way myself.  It

00:49:45.740 --> 00:49:49.660
feels like something big.
It feels like...

00:49:49.660 --> 00:49:53.740
this problem has spread across the entire
planet.

00:49:53.740 --> 00:50:00.000
And it feels like something that's difficult
for me to deal with.

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:03.220
But, we just entered

00:50:03.220 --> 00:50:06.800
after ten years of studying
the Lam Rim, we just

00:50:06.800 --> 00:50:13.020
entered the path for the
most capable people.  We

00:50:13.020 --> 00:50:16.720
are going to open that study

00:50:16.720 --> 00:50:21.040
with the idea of ​​bodhichitta.
What is bodhichitta?  It is

00:50:21.040 --> 00:50:27.400
not: enlightened mind.  Forget
about that incredibly bad translation.

00:50:27.400 --> 00:50:33.000
It is my wish that I may become a Buddha
to help countless living beings.

00:50:33.000 --> 00:50:37.080
And there is a direct experience of this,

00:50:37.080 --> 00:50:40.880
in the same way that there is a
direct experience of emptiness.

00:50:40.880 --> 00:50:44.600
There are parallel experiences that we

00:50:44.600 --> 00:50:48.600
must reach in this life.

00:50:48.600 --> 00:50:52.580
And again, you should be
meditating.

00:50:52.580 --> 00:51:00.220
We described an extraordinary...
what do you call it?  Discovery?

00:51:01.020 --> 00:51:04.560
Threshold experience,

00:51:05.760 --> 00:51:10.420
where you enter a deep state
of meditation, and,

00:51:10.420 --> 00:51:14.320
because time and space come
from seeds,

00:51:14.320 --> 00:51:16.740
if you can alter these seeds,

00:51:16.740 --> 00:51:20.840
then you can compact time
and space.

00:51:20.840 --> 00:51:25.160
In a meditation that lasts no more
than half an hour,

00:51:25.160 --> 00:51:30.320
you could actually visit every person
in the universe,

00:51:30.320 --> 00:51:33.780
including animals and bugs
and birds and fish,

00:51:33.780 --> 00:51:38.820
and you could communicate with each one
individually,

00:51:38.820 --> 00:51:40.860
within the half hour,

00:51:40.860 --> 00:51:44.220
and with each one you can make
a commitment.

00:51:44.220 --> 00:51:48.740
I mean, you know them, you see that each one
is suffering,

00:51:48.740 --> 00:51:54.340
each one is having a difficult life
and is worried about the future.

00:51:54.340 --> 00:51:57.680
You could go to each one separately
and say,

00:51:57.680 --> 00:52:00.520
"I've got you covered, take it easy."

00:52:00.520 --> 00:52:04.040
I used to work... when I was
at university I

00:52:04.040 --> 00:52:07.720
got a scholarship, but they told me I had to work a few hours a week.

00:52:07.720 --> 00:52:10.960
And it turned out to be 30 hours a week.  I was supposed to

00:52:12.200 --> 00:52:15.100
drive a truck,

00:52:15.100 --> 00:52:19.840
actually, first they sent me to a cafeteria
and told me I had to mop the floor.

00:52:19.920 --> 00:52:24.520
I quit within ten hours.  I quit on
the first day.

00:52:24.520 --> 00:52:30.020
Then they told me, "You can drive a truck."
I said, "That's fun. I'm going to drive a truck.

00:52:30.020 --> 00:52:33.440
I drove a truck for five years.

00:52:34.200 --> 00:52:36.980
We had a guy,

00:52:36.980 --> 00:52:41.700
a permanent employee of the university,
named Big John,

00:52:41.700 --> 00:52:48.740
his name was Big John. He was Polish, over six feet
tall, a huge guy.

00:52:49.360 --> 00:52:51.960
Everyone was scared of him when they saw him, they were
scared of him,

00:52:51.960 --> 00:52:55.580
but he was extremely sweet.

00:52:55.580 --> 00:53:02.220
He brought donuts to work and he was
from Trenton, New Jersey.

00:53:02.220 --> 00:53:03.960
Trenton.

00:53:03.960 --> 00:53:09.700
He did the best things for us and covered for us.
One day we broke the truck in half.

00:53:09.700 --> 00:53:13.040
We hit a tree with the truck
and broke it in half.

00:53:13.040 --> 00:53:19.240
And he covered for us: 'Oh, these bolts weren't tight enough.'"


00:53:19.240 --> 00:53:22.700
"I don't know what happened. The truck fell apart.
Do

00:53:22.700 --> 00:53:25.080
n't blame these kids."

00:53:25.080 --> 00:53:27.800
All they did was drive him around."

00:53:27.800 --> 00:53:32.940
Then he winked at us and said, "I've got you
covered."  "I've got you covered."

00:53:32.940 --> 00:53:36.280
I always think of him when I think
of bodhichitta.

00:53:36.280 --> 00:53:41.220
You're going to meet every living being
in the universe directly,

