I think the dumbest thing you can do
in your entire life

01:11:36.140 --> 01:11:39.720
is go to Paris and not buy a croissant.

01:11:40.240 --> 01:11:42.160
Okay? I'm just saying, there are

01:11:42.160 --> 01:11:45.180
probably other dumb things
you can do in your life,

01:11:45.180 --> 01:11:47.440
but for me, the ultimate dumbness

01:11:47.440 --> 01:11:50.820
is going to Paris and not going to a boulangerie,

01:11:50.820 --> 01:11:56.520
or at least buying a crepe
on the street

01:11:56.520 --> 01:12:00.140
with... what's that chocolatey stuff?

01:12:01.340 --> 01:12:03.020
Nutella, yes.

01:12:03.020 --> 01:12:06.360
Not eating a Nutella crepe.

01:12:06.360 --> 01:12:09.000
Going to Paris and not eating a Nutella crepe,

01:12:09.000 --> 01:12:12.660
then that shows you're crazy.

01:12:13.920 --> 01:12:15.980
If you're studying Lam Rim,

01:12:15.980 --> 01:12:21.420
if you've gotten this far in Lam Rim, and Geshehla
has been teaching it for ten years,

01:12:21.420 --> 01:12:24.880
and you'll finally get to the croissant,

01:12:24.880 --> 01:12:27.340
which is the bodhichitta experience, don't

01:12:27.340 --> 01:12:31.240
go crazy and leave Paris without one.  Eat it.

01:12:31.240 --> 01:12:37.540
Don't leave Lam Rim without having this experience. You'd
be a fool.

01:12:40.240 --> 01:12:45.980
We're done! With the croissant.
I think you want to make a presentation?

01:12:46.960 --> 01:12:52.680
No? I was assuming there might be
a croissant in that bag.

01:12:52.960 --> 01:12:59.240
Right. Tim Lowenhaupt is going to make
a formal presentation

01:12:59.280 --> 01:13:02.980
to Geshehla, my payment.

01:13:02.980 --> 01:13:07.840
Oh, is it a... bread...?
What do you call it?

01:13:07.840 --> 01:13:09.120
Seiji.

01:13:09.120 --> 01:13:13.060
What's it called?

01:13:13.060 --> 01:13:15.120
Chocolate bread, chocolate bread.

01:13:15.120 --> 01:13:18.940
Here, you have to divide it into three parts.

01:13:18.940 --> 01:13:22.420
And give me all three... I mean, no, just one.

01:13:22.420 --> 01:13:26.160
Very well. I have the chocolate bread.

01:13:26.160 --> 01:13:30.540
This is what you give to your teacher
when he teaches you about bodhichitta.

01:13:30.540 --> 01:13:33.480
So let's make a deal.

01:13:33.480 --> 01:13:35.700
For the next two months,

01:13:35.700 --> 01:13:42.340
work on that experience. Do the
dedication chapter in your meditation, from Shantideva.

01:13:42.340 --> 01:13:48.100
Try to work on having that experience.
The worst that can happen is that you'll at least

01:13:48.100 --> 01:13:52.040
plant seeds in your mind
to have the experience.

01:13:52.040 --> 01:13:53.600
Just pretend.

01:13:53.600 --> 01:13:59.180
Just sit and fantasize about it.
Fantasize  It's a good meditation.

01:13:59.180 --> 01:14:02.460
Imagine that you have this experience
of meeting

01:14:02.460 --> 01:14:05.280
each living being, one by one,

01:14:05.280 --> 01:14:09.460
and you make a personal commitment
to each one

01:14:09.460 --> 01:14:12.700
to care for them in the best possible way.

01:14:12.700 --> 01:14:13.460
Very good.

01:14:13.460 --> 01:14:18.760
See you at the next Lam Rim
for the Medicine Buddha. Yes!

